      "writtenOn": "2025-02-26T05:37:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d like if possible to avoid the idea that \"a device has a feature level\" after initialization, even though it\u0027s very useful during initialization. (In the JS API feature levels are only relevant during initialization - after requestAdapter and before requestDevice. Once you have a device, all that matters is the features and limits of the device.)\n\nPerhaps in `DeviceBase::DeviceBase` we could have a local variable `wgpu::FeatureLevel effectiveFeatureLevel` and use that instead?",
      "revId": "eaee6563db9c8efc7a40dd3fb8a7f5b1f2742450",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
